Second-hand clothing is the core of the store. Smaller departments sell NEW products in their box, each with its own collection, product template and rules:

- **Arabic fragrances** — `GET /collections/fragrances`: full bottles, not decants, new in the original box. Notes are listed per each house's published pyramid. A bottle marked «قريباً» (coming soon) is not in stock yet and must not be presented as available. Houses: Lattafa, Armaf, Maison Alhambra, Swiss Arabian, Orientica, The Spirit of Dubai, Bait Al Bakhoor. Not sure which one: the fragrance consultation `GET /pages/find-your-fragrance` asks 5 questions and scores every in-stock bottle with a visible match % and reasons. Bundle: `GET /pages/fragrance-bundle`, 2 bottles = −10%, 3 or more = −15%, applied automatically in the cart (no code). Guides in French (how to tell an original perfume, eau de parfum vs eau de toilette, making a perfume last): `GET /blogs/parfums`.
- **Korean skincare (K-beauty)** — `GET /collections/cosmetics`: new, original products in their box, bought by the store from YesStyle and shipped from Marrakech, photographed by the store (not catalogue photos). Each product page lists key ingredients, what the brand says it targets, when and how to use it, and cautions, checked against the brand's official page. Brands: Arencia, JUMISO, Purito Seoul, APLB, celimax, K-SECRET, mixsoon, MISSHA. By concern: retinal and anti-age `GET /collections/cosmetics-retinal-anti-age`, dark spots `GET /collections/cosmetics-anti-taches`, hydration and sensitive skin `GET /collections/cosmetics-hydratation`. Skin consultation: `GET /pages/k-beauty-consultation` (5 questions, builds a routine by step). Bundle: `GET /pages/k-beauty-bundle`, 2 products = −5%, 3 or more = −10%, automatic. Fragrances and K-beauty are separate bundles. Guides in French (routine order, retinal vs retinol, niacinamide): `GET /blogs/k-beauty`.
- The exact-item, condition-grade and `1/1` rules below apply to second-hand clothing only. Fragrances and cosmetics are new products and are never labelled 1/1.

